- Mkdir: make a directory
- ls or ls -lFs or ls -l etc...: list folders/files or show hidden files whether in time order or reverse order, there are many options.
- cd : change directory
- scp: secure copy, allows copying to other computers
- cd .. : changes directory for actions such as scp prompts that are done in original directory to then go back to stokes
- rm: removing files
- !$ : last done command
- ls f*: starts with f, "wild card"
- touch: creates a file and make it our current date
- cat: reading files
- cat ....... > longer.txt: puts cat file in listed other file
- less: view file content without opening with cat
- file: list types of files you have
- file.. *: describes type of file and the files type inside it
- wc: wordcount via lines/words/characters
- man: offers manual of any command listed after
-chmod: changes directory permissions


